# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
dist/
build/

# Test / lint / type / benchmark caches (generated at runtime)
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.benchmarks/

# Architecture-audit + dependency-graph artifacts (generated)
architect-output/
skills/**/scripts.svg

# Marketing kit (local only, not versioned)
docs/marketing/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local overrides
settings.local.json
*.local.md

# Session artifacts (generated at runtime, consumer-specific)
.active_plan
.compaction-snapshots/
.attestations/
cross-validation-output/
# Claude Code runtime dir of THIS repo acting as its own consumer
# (the shipped config lives in settings.json / settings.plugin.json at the root)
.claude/

# Study material, kept local (not part of the shipped cycle)
specs/

# Nested repository with its own remote — never a submodule of the cycle
codex-plugin-cc/

# Generated records content (scaffold dirs are tracked via .gitkeep)
records/grills/*.md
records/plans/*.md
records/implementations/**
records/reviews/*.md
records/releases/*.md
records/roadmap-runs/**
records/audits/*.md
records/adrs/*.md
records/honesty-gate/evidence/*.md
records/discoveries/plans/*.md
records/discoveries/blueprints/*.md
records/discoveries/snapshots/**
records/references/**
study-material/**
records/judge-codex/**
# The phase-transition stream. Per-session and per-machine by nature: what this
# repository's cycles did here says nothing to whoever clones it, and committing
# it would put one machine's run history in everyone's diff.
records/cycle-events.jsonl
# SOP run records: per-run and per-machine, like the phase-event stream. The
# PROCEDURE travels with the kit (records/sops/ stays versioned); what
# one machine did while following it does not.
records/sop-runs/**
!records/**/.gitkeep
!records/backlog.md

# Agent run logs (consumer-specific)
agents/**
!agents/.gitkeep
# EXCEPTION: the README describes the routing MECHANISM, not a domain, and
# install.sh copies it unconditionally. Keeping it ignored made every install
# performed outside this machine start with an empty `.claude/agents/` and a
# broken reference in rules/cycle-maintenance.md. The specialists stay out: each
# describes the repos of ONE ecosystem, and it is the project that derives its
# own. The eight the kit carried were removed on 2026-08-26 — they lived here for
# ages without ever being tracked, which is how a flag (--with-domain-agents)
# could deliver files that existed on one machine only.
!agents/README.md

# The kit's own two agents. They are mechanism, not domain specialists: they describe
# no repository and make no claim about any consumer's topology, which is the whole
# reason a specialist may not be versioned here. `squad_lead.py` invokes them through
# `claude -p` when the mechanical selector has no answer, and an agent that is not
# versioned reaches nobody — the exact failure the comment above records for the
# specialists that lived on one machine's disk.
!agents/squad-lead.md
!agents/squad-boss.md
